# Banana Bread

An American recipe in cups and ounces. The frontmatter doubles the
batch and converts everything to metric — no manual math required.
Currency costs scale automatically with the batch size.

## Ingredients (1 loaf)

flour = 3/2 cups
sugar = 3/4 cups
butter = 4 ounces
milk = 1/4 cups
bananas = 3 bananas
eggs = 2 eggs
baking_soda = 1 teaspoons
salt = 1/4 teaspoons
vanilla = 1 teaspoons

oven = 350 fahrenheit

## Cost

cost_flour = $0.50
cost_sugar = $0.30
cost_butter = $1.50
cost_milk = $0.25
cost_bananas = $0.75
cost_eggs = $0.60

total_cost = sum of cost_flour, cost_sugar, cost_butter, cost_milk, cost_bananas, cost_eggs
per_loaf = total_cost / @scale

Scaled batch costs {{total_cost}} total, or {{per_loaf}} per loaf.
You'll need {{flour}} of flour and {{butter}} of butter.
